  order: 1
---

The game world is made up of **maps** grouped into **areas**. An area is a collection of related maps, like all the rooms in Boo's Mansion. Most chapters have one or two areas.

<details>
    <summary>Paper Mario's areas</summary>

| Folder | Japanese | English |
|------|---------|---------|
| kmr | クリむら | Goomba Village |
| mac | まち | Toad Town |
| tik | まちのちか | Toad Town Tunnels |
| kgr | くじらのなか | Inside the Whale |
| kkj | きのこ城 | Princess Peach's Castle |
| hos | 星ふる丘 | Shooting Star Summit |
| nok | ノコノコむら | Koopa Village |
| trd | とりで | Koopa Bros. Fortress |
| iwa | 岩山 | Mt. Rugged |
| dro | カラカラタウン | Dry Dry Outpost |
| sbk | カラカラ砂漠 | Dry Dry Desert |
| isk | カラカラいせき | Dry Dry Ruins |
| mim | 迷いの森 | Forever Forest |
| obk | テレサハウス | Boo's Mansion |
| arn | あれの | Gusty Gulch |
| dgb | ドガボンの城 | Tubba Blubba's Castle |
| omo | ヘイホーのおもちゃばこ | Shy Guy's Toy Box |
| jan | ジャングル | Jade Jungle |
| kzn | 火山 | Mt. Lavalava |
| flo | フラワーランド | Flower Fields |
| sam | さむいさむい村 | Shiver City |
| pra | パラレルきゅうでん | Crystal Palace |
| kpa | クッパ城 | Bowser's Castle |
| osr | きのこ城そと | Outside Peach's Castle |
| end | エンディング | Ending |
| mgm | ミニゲーム | Minigames |
| gv | ゲームオーバー | Game Over |
| tst | テストマップ | Test Map |

Paper Mario names each area with three letters, and starts each map's name with its area's name, such as the map `kmr_20` in `kmr`. Your areas and maps don't have to follow this pattern.

</details>

Each map is a folder in its area's folder, such as `world/area/kmr/kmr_02/`. It holds:

- **The map**: its models, collision, zones, [markers](/papermario-dx/world/markers/), and [settings](#map-settings), which you edit in the map editor.
- **`main.c`**: the map's code, which controls what happens in the map. The game starts its `EVS_Main` EVT script when the player enters the map.
- **A header** named after the map, such as `kmr_02.h`, which the map's code includes.

## Creating the map

{% steps %}
1. In the Filesystem, right-click an area's folder in `world/area`, such as `kmr`, and select **New > Map**. To start a new area, right-click `world/area` and select **New > Area** instead. A new area comes with its first map.
2. Enter a name for the map. Diorama64 suggests the area's name followed by the first free number. A map's name can use letters, numbers, and underscores, and no two maps can share one.
3. Select **OK**.
{% /steps %}

## Refer to the map's objects

Each model, collider, and zone in the map has a constant, such as `MODEL_o101`, `COLLIDER_deilie`, and `ZONE_1`, that the map's code can refer to.

## Map settings

To change the map's settings, open the map and select nothing. The properties show the map's settings. In Star Rod without Diorama64, they're in the **Options** tab.

| Setting | What it sets |
| --- | --- |
| **Location** | Where the pause menu's map shows the player, such as `LOCATION_TOAD_TOWN`. Leave it empty to keep the location of the map the player came from. |
| **Tattle** | The message the player's partner says when it tattles on the map, such as `MSG_MapTattle_kmr_02`. |
| **Reverb** | The reverb on sound effects. The base game uses `1` in Gusty Gulch, `2` in Tubba Blubba's Castle, and `3` in Peach's Castle. |
| **Song variation** | Which version of some songs plays in the map, such as the special battle theme. |
| **Camera** | The camera's field of view, how near and far it draws, its background color, and whether it leads the player by looking ahead of them. |
| **World fog** and **Entity fog** | Fog over the map's models, and over its NPCs and entities. |

To give the map a background, select **Map > Has Background**, and choose the image with **Map > Change Background**.

The game sets up the location, camera, and fog as the map loads, before its `EVS_Main` starts, so the map's EVT scripts can change them, such as to move the camera in a [scene](/papermario-dx/world/scenes/).

If the tattle changes during the game, write a `get_tattle` function in the map's code that returns the message to use. It takes the place of **Tattle**.

```c
s32 get_tattle(void) {
    if (evt_get_variable(nullptr, GF_KPA16_ShutOffLava)) {
        return MSG_MapTattle_kpa_15_after;
    }
    return MSG_MapTattle_kpa_15_before;
}
```

## Testing the map

With the map's `main.c` or `map.xml` open, select **Game > Play**. The game starts in your map. If you last saved in that map, it starts where you saved. Otherwise, it starts at the map's first entry.
